{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>And Moses arose, and Joshua his minister.</b> Joshua was among the seventy elders mentioned above who beheld Elohim, and he was the greatest of them all." "<b>And you should ask</b> why Scripture mentions him here more than the others. And the Ramban, of blessed memory, wrote: it is possible to say that this teaches that all forty days that Moses was on the mountain, Joshua waited for him at the foot of the mountain, and because of this it mentioned him here — for he was his minister, accompanying him to the designated boundary on the mountain." "<b>And Moses went up unto the mount of Elohim.</b> To make known that all the while Moses was on the mountain, Joshua waited at the foot of the mountain. And a proof for this is that when Moses came down from the mountain, Scripture immediately mentioned Joshua, as it says (Exodus 32): ״וישמע יהושע את קול העם ברעה״ — and Joshua heard the voice of the people in shouting. And this verse teaches that Joshua was not with Israel in the camp, but was stationed at the foot of the mountain, waiting for Moses until his descent."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:03:40.051664533Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}